DSV 2.8 - Aug 2026
    Unfroze and refroze the bitstream to make very much needed changes :)
    Massive overhaul of the in-loop filtering
    Improved adaptive Rice coding via improved K parameter calculation
    Made memory allocations aligned
    Added color characteristics to metadata including the BC2 color space
    Removed static variables so users who want to multithread can have an easier time
    Added metadata validation to the decoder
    Changed the encoder's quant curve
    Improved CRF encoding
    Improved scene change detection
    Encoder tracks visual energy loss temporally to better allocate bits where needed
    Refactored and synced up the quantization for each band with the smoothing function in SBT
    Improved subband transforms
    Improved still image / intra frame compression
    Much better, smoother, motion estimation (+ chroma ME added)
    Encoder does a better job at mode selection during motion estimation
    Improved quantization

DSV 2.7 - May 16, 2025
    Better and faster motion estimation through better candidate MV selection and reducing diagonal searches
    Better rate control including the addition of CRF encoding (finally)
    More accurate inter/intra mode decision and RDO
    Temporal + anisotropic motion compensation for better subpixel motion
    Intra frame deringing filter
    Inter frame cleanup filter
    Fast local de-gradient / sharpening filter to reduce blurriness
    Haar is used at L3 rather than a longer filter now to reduce both ringing artifacts and also increase sharpness
    Simplified HZCC a bit
    Refactored decoding code
    YUV 4:1:0 support
